WEBVTT

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:05.330
January 10th (Saturday)

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.030
Yuki!

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.230
What are you doing there?

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.510
What do you want?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.300
You should've just come in.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.470
When did you get here?

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.140
Touya-kun...

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.490
You caught him?

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.180
He just went back.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.660
If only he knew you were coming, he could've waited for you.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.220
Then we could-

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.940
What did Touya-kun come here for?

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.110
You want to know?

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:41.450
Fujii-kun and I, we...

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.390
...kissed.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.890
I see.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.580
nemuri nasai ima wa tada

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.580
Sleep, for now

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:00.490
watashi no naka de doko ni mo ikanai de

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:00.490
Inside of me, and don't go anywhere

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:21.500
madoromi no fuchi de yureteru gunjou iro no yo

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:21.500
Through the slumbering ultramarine sky

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.020
majiwaru koto no nai hoshi wo sagashiteru

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.020
I am searching for stars that will never cross

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:34.720
anata wo motomeru yubisaki yami ni samayotte

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:34.720
These fingertips search for you, but are lost in darkness

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:43.600
mogaite mo nukedesenai ai no umi ni oboreteku

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:43.600
I try but I can't escape, and I drown in the sea of love

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:51.490
yawaranai toiki ni kokoro sae mo furueru

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:51.490
Your tender sigh makes my heart tremble

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:57.110
karamaru utsukushi kumo no ito no you

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:57.110
Seemingly entangled in the beautiful strands of a spider web

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.600
ugokenai no watashi wo yurushite

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.600
I cannot move, please forgive me

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.930
anata no ude ni dakarete nemuru

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.930
I am sleeping with your arms around me

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.150
nani mo kamo sutetatte ii

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:08.150
I don't mind losing anything else

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:15.680
ii kono mama no maboroshi nante zukuru no wa yamete

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:15.680
Stop pretending that you are a good girl

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.140
hontou no watashi wo mitsukete

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.140
Find the real me

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.220
zutto matteru

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.220
I'll be waiting forever

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:29.440
Since when?

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:33.070
That time.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:35.740
No, that time.

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:42.000
No, actually, when we first met at Echoes.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.510
I think.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:50.670
Page 19
It's called moving on to the next
 when you're bored of the previous.
Although, it usually seems like
I'm already bored before I even move on.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.810
I have no experience in matters of love.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:56.860
I've never even thought about them,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:00.310
and so I can't understand my own heart.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.240
When I did that, or that too,

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.870
Even that thing I said...

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.810
Now that I think about it, everything I did,

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.200
may have been because of my feelings for Fujii-kun.

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.520
But the time I truly realized it,

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.460
was when I retrieved your letter to Touya from Yayoi-san.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.380
"Why me," I thought...

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:19.600
Should I have torn it up and thrown it away?

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.940
I wondered, if I did that, could I still call myself a human being?

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.110
Why?

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.340
Why, Rina-chan?

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:29.730
Rina-chan, you read the letter?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.210
Yuki, that's-

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.430
Yayoi-san said that she gave the letter to him directly.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.860
Touya-kun said that he heard its contents from you.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:42.170
Touya-kun, you, and Yayoi-san...

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:44.530
The things you all say don't match...

00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.500
I'm getting so confused...

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.230
I'm starting to have more and more strange thoughts...

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.930
I know I shouldn't be so suspicious,

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:55.750
since these things have nothing to do with it...

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:02.300
But, I noticed the smell of Yayoi-san's perfume on Touya-kun.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.700
It also seems like Touya-kun's trying to hide something...

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.690
What are the three of you doing?

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:10.560
Who's being honest? Who's-

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.550
Lies. Lies.

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.390
Everyone's lying.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:17.400
Yayoi-san and Fujii-kun are both lying.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.040
I'm the only one who's telling the truth.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:20.860
My-

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.780
I once thought that things might not be this way.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.320
But, I can no longer think this is so anymore.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:32.310
The thought that Rina-chan and Touya-kun might be betraying me...

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.930
I tried my best not to think this way...

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.350
But, I guess I was right.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.210
Fujii-kun, he...

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.770
...requested to be my assistant just like before.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:52.320
You had a request?

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.460
Please hire me again.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.520
That's-

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.560
I'll go with you... to M3.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.110
Fujii-kun accepted it.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:02.830
No way-

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:03.820
It's the truth.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:06.450
No, anything but that.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.780
I definitely can't have that!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.070
It's too late, Yuki.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:14.160
Fujii-kun has already accepted my feelings.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.250
I don't want to hear any more!

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.120
I don't want to hear any more!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.250
What are you going to do?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:20.660
What are you going to do to me?

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.850
I don't want to... hear...

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:23.790
You'll hit me?

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.800
Go ahead.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.980
Go ahead and hit me, Yuki.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:32.450
If you really love Fujii-kun, then don't hold back.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.090
Come on, use those hands-

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.130
Yuki...

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:45.390
What... are you doing?!

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:48.300
Yuki!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:50.120
Yuki!

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.400
Let go!

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.210
Let go!

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:03.230
I can't!

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.140
I can't hit you!

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:10.050
Because... you're also someone I love!

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.400
You dummy.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.520
For an idol to go as far as to injure herself...

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.430
Do you really love him that much?

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:28.930
The most important person in your life is Fujii-kun, am I right?

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.430
Yet, for me to-

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.460
I understand.

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:38.210
Are you fine with simply enduring whatever comes?

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.080
Yuki?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:41.770
I'm not enduring anything.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:44.800
All I do, is wait.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:48.610
All I do is wait, forever, and ever.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.030
It's all I've been doing.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.620
What if things can't go back the way they used to be?

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.600
I'll still wait.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.800
You'll still wait?

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:00.520
Until I die, and disappear from this world.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.540
We're complete opposites, aren't we?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:08.550
Me, you, and Fujii-kun.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.160
Fujii-kun and you are alike in many ways.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.660
Just like siblings.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:15.100
That's why you like each other.

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:19.520
And that's also why I won't let go of Fujii-kun.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.010
But, I understand.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.950
If that's the case, I'll wait too.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:26.800
I'll wait...

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.560
It's not like I told him I love him or anything.

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:30.660
There's still a long way to go.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:34.400
For now, I'll set my sights on the upcoming Venus festival,

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:36.570
and do my best.

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.430
Yuki, you too... right?

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.940
I decided not to participate in the Venus festival.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.080
That's what I told Ogata-san-

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.270
What are you saying?!

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.730
Do you have any idea why I-

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.360
If you say that again,

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.550
I'll be the one who'll hit <i>you</i>.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.390
Hey, Yuki.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:00.990
Promise me.

00:08:00.990 --> 00:08:04.290
From now on, we'll be rivals both at work and in our private lives.

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.520
You'll work hard in order to beat me.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.790
I'm serious.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:13.060
This isn't a suggestion or a discussion.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:17.620
This is my last order as your senior.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.880
Follow it, Yuki.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.310
It's gotten pretty late now.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:31.770
I made the two of them wait for me in the car.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:33.550
I'm sorry.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.400
Look at you, you're apologizing already.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.070
Ah, sorry-

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.220
Do you need a ride?

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.270
Well, I guess I'll be going.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.570
Farewell, Yuki.

00:09:10.710 --> 00:09:11.980
Yuki-san.

00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.110
Where are you right now?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.280
You're at Touou Television?

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.940
Understood. I'll be right there.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:29.750
Yuki-san!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:51.630
President, Yuki-san's here.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.150
Yayoi-san.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.130
I don't want to go back yet.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.420
Could you drive me around for a while?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.700
It'll affect tomorrow's schedule.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:17.800
If you promise me that you won't cry
anymore today, then I'll accompany you.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.510
I understand.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.830
Off we go.

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.790
He was never able to get back on his feet.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.590
There's no meaning to that!

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.050
Ogata-san must be horribly mad at me, right?

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.210
Nope.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:14.240
If he was really mad, he wouldn't have let you off with just this.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:16.650
I guess so.

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:20.820
It's almost time to go back.

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:22.310
Yes.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.270
Hello? It's me.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:58.310
I managed to find some time to go and give Rina my support today.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:01.030
I'm sorry I didn't contact you earlier.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.240
And, uh...

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.370
Rina-chan was unexpectedly full of energy.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:09.870
And then, this will be quite sudden, but I got a new job.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:11.620
Somehow, I'm Rina-chan's assistant again-

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:24.660
What did he say?

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:30.120
Eh? What, he mortgaged the painting and can't get it back?

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:32.960
I'll call you back later.

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:34.890
Enter.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:37.290
Good morning.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.320
Ooh, how punctual you are.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.230
Please take care of me from now on.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.960
How convenient.

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:44.240
I listened to your album.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:46.200
It's not very good.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.310
It's all over the place, and I see no unifying theme.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.330
I guess Ei-chan's reached his limit!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.440
I'm afraid our company can't go forward with this.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.230
I'm going to leave this to our professional composers,

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.200
so this album will be put on hold for a while.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:12:59.670
Who is he?

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:01.930
I'm Fujii.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:04.450
He's my personal assistant.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.120
I disapprove.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:08.870
I'm employing him out of my own wallet.

00:13:08.870 --> 00:13:10.630
He won't trouble you.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:13.840
You can't go on doing whatever you want here, you know.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.460
Menou-san's girl... her name is Natsuko, isn't it? She's-

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:19.310
But that girl...

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:23.940
That's because Menou can't sing without that girl beside her.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.030
It's a special case.

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:28.010
Me too. I cannot sing if he's not here with me.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.860
I can't live without him.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:36.510
Since he'll have nothing to do with our
production company, do whatever you want.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:38.370
Yes.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.710
Be sure not to give the wrong impression.

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:42.380
You can rest assured on that matter.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:44.320
I don't think you'll be needing a manager for now.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.200
By the way, Menou is the one who'll go to the Venus Festival.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.080
Don't get the wrong impression on that either.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:53.520
I understand.

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.420
What would you like me to do for now?

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:01.320
Let's see, Menou should be recording her album at this point,

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.730
could you help her with the vocals?

00:14:03.870 --> 00:14:07.110
She's at the studio that used to belong to your brother. You know where it is.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.910
I'll let her know you're coming.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.790
It'll be good publicity for her, with you participating.

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.390
Are you putting all of them in?

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:27.120
That's right. Everything Ogata Rina from the last half-year.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:31.830
We'll take what we've found together, and carve it in just as it is.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.770
It'll be a treasure chest of an album.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:36.750
It could even be a Pandora's box. What do you think?

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:38.080
I like it.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:39.180
Let's do it.

00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.040
We'll be in the same company from now onwards, please take care of me.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.610
Our sentiments also, please take care of us too.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.930
Manager, you?!

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:06.170
My name's Muromachi, and I'm now in charge of Ms. Touin Sarii.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.340
That single of mine.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.260
Menou-san will be writing it for me.

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:14.220
Right.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:17.780
Positively speaking, we're blank slates,

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:19.660
and so we can sing songs written by anyone.

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:22.410
Things must be tough for you, Rina-chan.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.100
Your colors are already set in stone.

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:29.490
If they're not your brother's songs, you must have problems with them.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:32.180
That's not true. After all, I'm-

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:42.360
Don't tell me she's... underaged?

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:44.920
She actually turned 20 last month,

00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:46.610
but she's 18 on her profile.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.100
It's a secret.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.560
What about you? I mean, you were-

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:54.270
I turned into an adult two years ago.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.930
It's no longer a secret, though.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:59.360
So you were older than me...

00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:03.970
Sarii, she...

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:06.940
The President knows that she probably won't make it.

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:08.940
Since the days of the Sakura-dan...

00:16:09.310 --> 00:16:11.710
...she's the only one who still hasn't realized that yet.

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:13.880
No, she probably does realize it.

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:15.120
Then why-

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:16.770
She won't listen.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.340
"I'm not stopping, I'm going solo," she said...

00:16:19.550 --> 00:16:21.830
You could say that she's very optimistic.

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:25.970
I, on the other hand, can only face reality pessimistically.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:27.610
And you're fine with that?

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.260
I'm not talking about her, but you.

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:35.100
My dream has already been fulfilled.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.790
I had a concert at the Arena!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.420
I wonder if this is something you should say to President Kanzaki.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:47.650
Because you were all professionals, your futures will be bleak should things stay this way.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:52.890
That's straying into the realm where
children like us won't understand a thing...

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:56.760
If nothing can be said, then we can only cheer for her.

00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:00.060
Ah, it's time.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:04.920
We're headed to a reception for the evening paper and the youth paper.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.980
I'm sorry for what has happened in the past.

00:17:14.400 --> 00:17:16.110
Excuse me, Rina-chan.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.260
I'm sorry.

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:19.690
You sure took your time.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.410
I wasn't able to grab hold of a taxi for a while...

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.140
It's waiting for us down there now.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:25.330
A taxi?

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.760
Didn't I tell you to hire a car?

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:28.920
About that...

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:32.190
I didn't have a permit, so...

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:35.820
Why's that? We have a contract with this company, don't we?

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:39.760
The person at the reception asked the President.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:43.750
Hiring a car costs money, and so it didn't work out...

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.430
Right.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:47.680
I'm sorry, but send the Taxi away.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:20.450
Hello.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.450
Ah. Um...

00:18:26.920 --> 00:18:27.940
Do you remember me?

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:32.590
Ah, we met at Koukai Street!

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:37.680
Let's get this started. Sing it once for me.

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.160
Let's go with it, Rina.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:53.930
If it's difficult to sing, we can change it.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.450
I never said it was difficult to sing.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.110
The way the melody goes just wasn't very comfortable to sing.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:01.310
Hey, are you listening to me, Nii-san?!

00:19:01.310 --> 00:19:03.700
Eh, did you say something?

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.170
Do you have a moment?

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:25.600
Right before the hook when your voice doubles, the third note of the second measure.

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:30.080
Only one of the voices dropped a flat. I think we should fix it.

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.060
Where?

00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.080
Doesn't really matter, does it?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.450
I don't think it's very tasteful at all, though.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.360
Well, let's just take it out then.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:52.170
We'll do that.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:58.620
In that case, how about I sing that in unison for you, and we mix that into the chorus?

00:19:58.790 --> 00:20:00.070
Do whatever you want.

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.250
Sounds good. Go ahead.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:08.680
As long as you like it, Rina.

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:17.650
Thank you for that time.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:23.690
You remember now?

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:26.150
Yeah, we met at Koukai Street-

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:27.160
I guess not.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:29.730
Was I your savior-goddess?

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:38.780
So you were just about to go to the concert.

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:40.810
Yes.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:44.080
You had a bouquet. You're a fan of Morikawa Yuki?

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:45.930
Is that weird?

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:47.750
Just unexpected.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:51.220
An adult like you going after an idol like that.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:54.020
We're going out.

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.710
Sounds like a lie, doesn't it?

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:04.030
It really does... sound like a lie.

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.010
Hey, would you like to listen to it-

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:15.250
You're annoying.

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:26.790
You're the one who's annoying.

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:29.880
What do you want?

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:32.280
I'd like you to check something.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:35.140
Didn't I already say you were free to do whatever you wanted?

00:21:35.430 --> 00:21:37.630
Understood. I'll do whatever I want.

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:42.170
Where do you live now?

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:45.320
In Ibukichou...

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:14.180
What's wrong, Yuki?

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:19.810
Ogata-san, why?

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:36.760
Welcome back.

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:40.040
Why

00:22:49.570 --> 00:22:56.110
watashi ni itsumo anata wa yasashii

00:22:49.570 --> 00:22:56.110
You have always been kind to me

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:02.680
sono yasashisa ga fuan ni suru

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:02.680
But this kindness makes me insecure

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:11.520
unmei no ito hodokenai you ni

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:11.520
This string of fate, I'll retie it over and over

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:18.130
nando mo musubi naoshite

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:18.130
So that it will never come loose

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:26.500
tsugi ni au yakusoku dekinai mama

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:26.500
I don't want to hear you say goodbye

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:36.450
wakare no kotoba mada kikitaku wa nai yo

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:36.450
Until we make promises to meet again

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:44.190
aenai yoru ni yume de aetara

00:23:36.780 --> 00:23:44.190
Even if we can't meet tonight, 
if I can see you in my dreams

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:52.100
ashita ga tsurakute mo waratte irareru

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:52.100
Even if tomorrow is difficult I'll be able to smile

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:59.570
donna ni tooku hanarete ite mo

00:23:52.100 --> 00:23:59.570
No matter how far apart we may become

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:09.550
tsunagatte ireru to shinjite iru

00:23:59.840 --> 00:24:09.550
I believe that we will still be connected together

00:24:21.880 --> 00:24:23.180
Page 20

00:24:23.790 --> 00:24:25.380
Love is not rational.

00:24:25.780 --> 00:24:27.920
The lovers who said this,

00:24:27.920 --> 00:24:30.780
were poets, commentators, and philosophers.

00:24:31.420 --> 00:24:32.750
White Album.
